# Changelog

All major changes to bronko will be documented in this file

## [v0.1.6] - 08/23/2026

- Introduced SOR_adj, which takes the SOR score and subtracts a score that increases as the minor allele has more supporting reads and is futher above the baseline noise for that window. --sor-adj-multiplier controls the strength of this adjustment.
- Indel reconstruction is now off by default and can be enabled with --indels (previously --no-indels was used to disable)
- Indel reconstruction is more robust and no longer reconstructs large regions from the 5' and 3' ends of the sequences
- General bug fixes and minor tweaks to variant calling, psuedo-mapping
- Ambiguous bases (non ACTG) are now handled and ignored
- Consensus generation no longer reverts to reference
- Indexing now filters duplicate buckets within an individual genome
- Baseline noise model now incorporates model of sequencing error (useful in cases of low sequencing depth where error falls below the min-kmers threshold)
- Bug fixes for paired end read counting
- SOR default is now lower (3)

## [v0.1.5] - 07/30/2026
- Added `--bucket-filter` which allows for users to specify a spaced-k-mer pattern when using the `call` command. bronko will only use  positions that are filtered within the kmer, improving computational performance while potentially losing some sensitivity. Enables use of split-kmer (ska) like patterns (i.e 00100 for k=5) and others. 
- Added .log file to all `call` runs. 

# [v0.1.4] - 07/22/2026
- Added indel reconstruction and variant calling ability for novel indels and two-stage mapping approach as default (toggleable with `--no-indels`)
- Coosensus sequence generation now reflects the reconstructed genome sequence
- Improved performance of call command and other quality of life updates

## [v0.1.3] - 02/06/2026
- Added `--file-input` for both build and call command to allow users to use txt with samples as input (more detail in wiki)
- Improved performance of build command with many genomes
- Other logging and path enhancements

## [v0.1.2] - 01/27/2026
- Minor bug fixes
- Sample will still be processed even if no sequencing depth or mapping information 

## [v0.1.1] - 01/15/2026
- Added consensus sequence reporting output with `--consensus`
- Only saving _counts.txt file from kmc with `--keep-kmer-info`
- Default min minor allele frequency is now 0.01, can still be set using `min-af`

## [v0.1.0] - 11/11/2025
- First major release of bronko, corresponding to first manuscript
- Updated defaults for multiple variant calling parameters, introduced multiple others to allow more control over variant calls
- By default now significant strand balance issues will be filtered

## [v0.0.3] - 10/28/2025
- Introduced baseline noise filter using streaming version of modified thompson tau filter

## [v0.0.2] - 10/20/2025
- Fixed major bug when counting kmers for paired end reads 
- Introduced SOR strand filter replacement for previous naive method 

## [v0.0.1] - 10/16/2025
First public pre-release of bronko

### Added 
- bronko call
- bronko build
